# `@sonaraem/orpc`

## Procedure Chain

```
publicProcedure
  ├── protectedProcedure    → context.session (dashboard auth)
  │     └── approvedProcedure → + DB isApproved && !banned
  ├── adminProcedure        → context.adminSession + role === "admin"
  └── cronOrAuthProcedure   → session OR SONARAEM_CRON_SECRET
```

- `protectedProcedure`: dashboard session → `context.session.user.id`
- `approvedProcedure`: same + live DB check via `assertUserApproved()` — use for all user data routes
- `adminProcedure`: admin session only → `context.adminSession` (separate cookie from dashboard)
- `cronOrAuthProcedure`: accepts session OR `X-Organize-Secret`/`Authorization: Bearer <SONARAEM_CRON_SECRET>`

## Context

`createContext()` resolves **both** sessions in parallel:

- `session` — from `dashboardAuth.api.getSession()` (`/api/auth`, `sonaraem-dashboard` cookie)
- `adminSession` — from `adminAuth.api.getSession()` (`/api/admin-auth`, `sonaraem-admin` cookie)

## Router Structure

```
src/routers/
  public/
    waitlist.ts       signup, status (HMAC token)
    organize.ts       cronOrAuthProcedure
  protected/
    index.ts          redeemInvite (protectedProcedure only)
    playlists.ts      approvedProcedure
    tracks.ts
    pipeline.ts       streamStatus uses eventIterator for SSE
    ...
  admin/
    waitlist.ts       approve, reject, resendInvite, bulk ops
    users.ts
    stats.ts
```

## Adding a Route

1. Zod schemas in `packages/common/src/schemas/{entity}/`
2. Handler in `packages/orpc/src/routers/{scope}/{domain}.ts`
3. Export from the router's `index.ts`
4. Optionally add `.meta({ openapi: { ... } })` for the OpenAPI spec

## Client Usage

```typescript
import { orpc } from "@/shared/api/orpc";
import { useQuery, useMutation } from "@tanstack/react-query";

const { data } = useQuery(orpc.playlists.list.queryOptions());
const { mutate } = useMutation(orpc.admin.waitlist.updateStatus.mutationOptions({ onError: toastError }));
```

## Error Handling

Throw `ORPCError` directly from handlers/middleware with a typed code — never a bare `Error`:

```typescript
import { ORPCError } from "@orpc/server";

if (!row || row.banned || !row.isApproved) {
  throw new ORPCError("FORBIDDEN");
}
```

Codes in use: `UNAUTHORIZED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `BAD_REQUEST`, `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`, `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR`. Domain errors that originate in `@sonaraem/common` services (e.g. `PipelineCancelledError`) stay plain `Error` subclasses there — only the oRPC layer translates into `ORPCError`.

## Rate Limiting

- Applied globally via `rateLimitMiddleware` on `publicProcedure`
- In-memory per process — not shared across API instances (see README)

## Tests

```bash
pnpm --filter @sonaraem/orpc test
```

## CORS

Applied globally in `apps/api/src/app/api/[[...rest]]/route.ts`. Auth routes use `apps/api/src/lib/auth-route.ts`. Never add per-route CORS elsewhere.
